I'm rather astonished, too.  A mumak *cannot* do more than 60 points of
damage in a single round (and will usually, even on a double hit, do
about 30-40).

*crunches numbers*

OK. A level 11 human wizard has (10 + 2 + 10d8 + 10d2) = (10d8 + 10d2 +
12) = 32 to 112 hit points (ignoring constitution modifiers, which isn't
that unreasonable to do for the lower levels). That's an average of 72
hp. (An elven wizard will average 66 hit points at level 11.)

So, yeah. A run of poor luck on hit point rolls, or not being at full
health.
